# Kontakt 8.13 at 100 % (shoot.sh, DPI=96), oracle run 2026-11-25: where each field's words sit
# (gen.py fields(); 72x20 controls, the line "Lowpass 4"). `first` is the first column of ink
# from the control's left edge; `width` the line's ink width; `rows` the first and last ink rows.
# Font 0 and an unset font draw as the stock 9 px pixel font. TEXT_ALIGNMENT 0 = left,
# 1 = centre, 2 = right; unset is left for menus, buttons and switches. A menu's words run under
# its arrow (right inset 1), a button's and a switch's stop 7 px from the edge.
# Fonts 1 and 13 on a field draw as a label in that font does.
# A lit button or switch in the stock font draws the same pixel font in ink 0x181818.
# $CONTROL_PAR_TEXTPOS_Y on a button or switch moves the words down from their centred place
# (0 = unset; 6 moves them 6 px lower), lit or not.
# KONTRA checks: crates/app/ui-view/src/tests.rs, crates/app/host/tests/ui.rs.
kind    font   align  first  width  rows
menu    stock  0      7      44     9-17
menu    stock  1      16     35     9-17
menu    stock  2      26     44     9-17
button  stock  0      7      44     9-17
button  stock  1      13     44     9-17
button  stock  2      20     44     9-17
switch  stock  0      7      44     9-17
switch  stock  1      13     44     9-17
switch  stock  2      20     44     9-17
button  1      0      8      54     8-16
button  1      1      9      54     8-16
button  1      2      10     54     8-16
button  13     0      8      48     8-15
button  13     1      12     48     8-15
button  13     2      17     37     8-15
menu    1      0      8      44     8-16
menu    13     0      8      48     8-15
# The centred stock menu line measures 35 px: its right end runs under the arrow.
# Open in KONTRA: font 1 on a field is 57 px against 54 and font 13 sits one row lower at the end.
